+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` counts the unbroken streak of losing trades closed within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), most-recent-trade first, stopping at the first trade that isn't a loss.
+If that streak reaches `trade_limit` or more, trading will stop for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+A trade counts as a loss when its close profit is below `required_profit` (defaults to `0.0`).
+
+This is evaluated both per-pair (locking only the affected pair) and bot-wide across all pairs (locking every pair), unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which disables the bot-wide check and only locks the individual pair.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of long losses.
+
+Unlike `StoplossGuard`, any losing trade counts towards the streak - not just trades that exited via stoploss - and a single winning (or breakeven) trade resets the streak.
+
+The below example stops trading for a pair (and, since `only_per_pair` is not set, for the whole bot) for 12 candles after 3 losing trades in a row within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 #### Cooldown Period
 
 `CooldownPeriod` locks a pair for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) after exiting, avoiding a re-entry for this pair for `stop_duration` minutes.
